### Why (v1.1.0 collision resolution)
This was a design collision: main and PR #2092 both independently bumped the skill to **v1.1.0** with different physics. Main's v1.1.0 added the Deutsch CTC (closed-timelike-curve) oracle domain (Deutsch 1991, Aaronson-Watrous 2009). PR #2092's v1.1.0 added the TSVF / weak-value retrocausal oracle domain. The two share an identical meta-workflow (real-citation-grounded speculative physics, 14-walls table, parsimony/capability scoring, root-break cascade) but cover distinct physics domains. The collision was resolved by combining BOTH physics domains into a single merged **v1.2.0**, so neither the CTC content nor the TSVF content was lost.

